---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';

const ids = ['harnesses.claudeCode.permissionModes', 't3code.queueSteer', 't3code.browser'];
const planPrompt = `Before you change anything, write a numbered plan: what you will build, which files you will touch, and every place where the request could mean two things.
Then stop and wait for my answer. Do not start until I say go.
If a new fork comes up while you build, ask me in one line and carry on with the parts that do not depend on it.`;
const reviewPrompt = `Build me a review page for this project, for development only, never shipped.
- List every screen the last change touched, with a screenshot of each.
- Under each screenshot, a notes box.
- Save each note to notes/review.md, with the screen it belongs to and the date.
- At the start of every turn, read notes/review.md, fix what is open, and mark each note done.`;
---
<Journey chapter="turn" first="once" title="Your turn" description="Ways to step in before, during, and after an agent builds—and how to have it build a better review tool for you.">
  <Step id="once" title="If you only speak at the start">
    <p>Halfway through a task, the agent hits an ambiguity—should paused members be hidden or greyed out? It guesses, spends twelve turns building on that guess, and leaves <a href={url('journey/proof/')}>the review tray from step 12</a> empty until it is too late.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="plan" title="Approve the plan first">
    <p>Ask for a short plan before any files are edited. The agent pauses at the check and waits for your go-ahead—read step 3 before you approve it.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="plan" data-val="go" aria-pressed="false">Go ahead</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="plan" data-val="change" aria-pressed="false">Change step 3</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt title="Plan first, then wait" compact>{planPrompt}</CopyPrompt>
      <p>Claude Code also has a plan mode among its permission modes: <Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.permissionModes" />.</p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="ask" title="Answer questions mid-run">
    <p>Instead of guessing—or stalling the whole job—the agent drops a question on your tray and keeps working on everything else. That one decision stays open until you answer.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-do="answer">Answer it: greyed out</button>
    </div>
    <More title="In T3 Code">
      <p><Fact id="t3code.queueSteer" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="pin" title="Point right at the result">
    <p>Typing “the badge looks off” leaves the model guessing which of the two badges you mean. Pinning a note directly on the screenshot attaches the exact location, so the fix hits the right element on the first try.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="pin" data-val="type" aria-pressed="false">Type “the badge looks off”</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="pin" data-val="pin" aria-pressed="false">Pin a note on it</button>
    </div>
    <More title="In T3 Code">
      <p><Fact id="t3code.browser" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="build" title="Have it build your review tool">
    <p>When you review the same kind of output repeatedly, ask the agent to build a small review page for you. Your comments save straight to a notes file that the agent reads at the start of its next turn.</p>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt title="A review page" compact>{reviewPrompt}</CopyPrompt>
      <p>This guide uses one itself (<code>site/integrations/comments/</code>): in the dev server you highlight text on any page to leave a note, each note saves to a file, and <code>pnpm comments</code> lists open notes for the agent.</p>
    </More>
    <Next from="turn" more={[{ href: 'wiki/giving-feedback/', text: 'Giving feedback' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The example feature, ambiguity, and turn counts are illustrative.</p>
    <Verified ids={ids} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
